"""
vip -- very important papers: from one paper, the tree of the most important
works that cite it, of the most important works that cite those, and so on.

Usage:
    vip PAPER [options]

PAPER is a DOI, an arXiv id, an OpenAlex id (W...), or a key of the --bib
files, as for citing (https://github.com/laussy/citing, which vip needs).

How the tree grows: the works citing the paper are read from OpenAlex, ranked,
and the best N are kept; each of them is treated in the same way, down to the
given depth. A work is shown once, at its first place in the tree; when it is
again among the best citers of another work, a "see [n]" line says so. All
counts come from OpenAlex, so that they can be compared with one another.

Truncation:
    -d, --depth D         generations below the paper (default 2)
    -n, --top N[,N2,...]  works kept under each work; a list gives one number
                          per generation, and the depth is then its length
                          unless -d says otherwise (default 5)
    -r, --rank BY         rate: citations per year since publication (default)
                          recent: citations in this year and the two before
                          cites: all citations
        --min-cites N     leave out works cited fewer than N times
        --since YEAR      leave out works published before YEAR
        --until YEAR      leave out works published after YEAR
        --type TYPES      only these OpenAlex types, comma-separated (review,
                          article, preprint, book-chapter, ...). By default all
                          but erratum, paratext and retraction
        --topic WORDS     only works with WORDS in their title or abstract
                          (an OpenAlex search: it costs more of the budget)
        --no-self         leave out works sharing an author with the work
                          they are placed under
        --max N           stop when the tree holds N works (default 300)
        --pool N          citing works read per work before ranking: the N
                          most cited, plus, unless --rank cites, the N most
                          cited of the last five years (default 200)

Output:
    -b, --bib FILES       BibTeX file(s), comma-separated: works get their key
    -f, --format FMT      text (default), json, dot (Graphviz), wiki (nested
                          list of {{key}}), keys (bib keys, one per line), ids
                          (DOI or arXiv:ID of works with no key)
    -o, --output FILE     write there instead of stdout; a .svg, .pdf or .png
                          is drawn by Graphviz's dot from the dot format
        --no-links        no "see [n]" lines, and in the drawing only the
                          tree's own edges
    -W, --width N         cut text lines at N characters (default: the
                          terminal's width; lines are not cut when piped)
        --fresh           do not use the cache (~/.cache/vip, answers younger
                          than 7 days are reused)
        --mailto EMAIL    contact for the OpenAlex polite pool (or env
                          VIP_MAILTO); nothing is sent without it
        --openalex-key K  OpenAlex API key (or env OPENALEX_API_KEY)
    -q, --quiet           no progress or summary on stderr
    -V, --version         the version
    -h, --help            this message

Text columns: [n] number in the tree, year, citations, the ranking figure
(per year, or recent), marks (R review, P preprint, * shares an author with
the work above it), then the bib key (or the DOI), first author and title.

Defaults: ~/.viprc (or the file named by env VIP_RC) holds options as on the
command line; --bib, --mailto and --openalex-key are also taken from
~/.citingrc when ~/.viprc does not give them.
"""

